<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:windows">
<!--
  GH-1969. clang -O2 for Win64 gives a leaf float function an eight-byte frame
  with push rax / pop rax. halfsel is
  float f(void *p, unsigned i) { double d = *(double *)((char *)p + 0x108);
  return ((float *)&d)[i]; }: the spill overwrites the pushed slot, so at the
  ret rax holds the double's bits and xmm0 the selected float. scaled stores
  two computed floats into the frame and returns one by index. Both returned
  rax, losing the index parameter and the indexed read.
  Controls: pushfq; pop rax returns the flags, a pop of the third argument
  beside an xmm0 that is only stored returns that argument, and pair builds an
  eight-byte struct { float f; int i; } in the frame and pops it into rax, the
  struct's return register, while xmm0 still holds the float it stored.
-->
